      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"While it is natural to prioritize our own communities, viewing foreign aid as a mere luxury ignores the profound moral duty we owe to the world's most vulnerable human beings who suffer preventable hardship. Sending resources abroad to fight radicalization, support democratic institutions, and preserve critical global health systems safeguards the very borders and foundations that protect our local population from future catastrophes. Ultimately, our generosity abroad is not an act of charity for others, but a strategic investment in the safety, stability, and shared future of all humanity, including our own descendants.",
